.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-JOB 1 "2026-09-20" "ShardPost 0.26.1" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-job \- plan, apply and watch maintenance jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl plan
.RB [ \-classes
.IR list ]
.RB [ \-mailbox
.IR mailbox ]
.RB [ \-uids
.IR list " | " \-deleted ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I kind account
.br
.B shardpostctl plan show
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I plan-id
.br
.B shardpostctl apply
.RB [ \-wait ]
.RB [ \-poll
.IR duration ]
.RB [ \-idempotency-key
.IR key ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I plan-id
.br
.B shardpostctl check
.RB [ \-wait ]
.RB [ \-poll
.IR duration ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl job list
.RB [ \-account
.IR account ]
.RB [ \-state
.IR state ]
.RB [ \-limit
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-after
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl job show
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.I job-id
.br
.B shardpostctl job wait
.RB [ \-poll
.IR duration ]
.I job-id
.br
.B shardpostctl job cancel
.I job-id
.SH DESCRIPTION
Everything that runs long or cannot be undone runs as a job. Jobs live in
the shared admin store, survive restarts and are taken over by another
server if the one running them dies, continuing at their last checkpoint.
.PP
Dangerous work is done in two steps.
.B plan
computes what the job
.I would
do and stores that plan; nothing is changed yet.
.B apply
runs the plan, once, and only while it is valid
.RI ( jobs.plan_ttl_seconds ,
one hour by default). Before the first write the job compares the account
with the plan: if it drifted, the job ends without changing anything.
.PP
.B check
needs no plan: it runs the read-only index check on an account.
.SS Kinds
.TP
.B index_check
Role
.BR diagnose .
Checks the index and reports findings. Repairs nothing. This is what
.B check
runs.
.TP
.B scrub
Role
.BR repair .
Checks and repairs.
.B \-classes
selects what may be repaired:
.IR deliveries ", " moves ", " retired ", " uncovered ", " entries ", "
.IR refs ", " orphans ", " unknown ", " quota .
Without the flag every class is repaired.
.TP
.B quota_recalc
Role
.BR repair ,
locks the account. Counts the usage from the index again and stores it.
.TP
.B acl_reconcile
Role
.BR repair .
Writes missing share pointers at the grantees and removes pointers that
no longer carry rights.
.TP
.B fts_rebuild
Role
.BR repair ,
locks the account. Drops the full-text index and builds it again from
every message. It has no checkpoint: after a takeover it starts over.
.TP
.B mailbox_delete
Role
.BR delete ,
locks the account. Deletes the mailbox named by
.B \-mailbox
with its children. INBOX is refused.
.TP
.B expunge
Role
.BR delete .
Removes the messages named by
.B \-uids
or, with
.BR \-deleted ,
every message that carried
.I \eDeleted
when the plan was made. Only messages that still have the UID and GUID
from the plan are removed, at most 40000 per plan.
.TP
.B purge
Role
.BR delete ,
locks the account. Withdraws shares in both directions, deletes the
learning jobs and every object of the account. The identity itself (LDAP)
is not touched: if the account logs in again, it gets an empty INBOX.
.SS The account lock
Jobs marked above as "locks the account" take the same lock an import
uses. While it is held, IMAP and POP3 answer "Mailbox maintenance in
progress", LMTP answers
.IR "451 4.2.1" ,
and other jobs and imports stay out. Sessions that were already open
notice within five seconds and are disconnected. The job waits
.I jobs.settle_seconds
(10 by default) after locking before it writes, so deliveries in flight
can finish.
.PP
If the account is already locked when a job starts, the job waits in
state
.I running
with the phase "waiting for the account lock" and tries again every lease
period, up to
.I jobs.plan_ttl_seconds
after it was created.
.SS States
.IR queued ", " running ", " succeeded ", " partially_failed ", " failed ", "
.IR cancel_requested ", " cancelled .
.B job cancel
stops a queued job at once and a running one at its next safe point; what
it already did is not rolled back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-classes " list"
Repair classes of
.BR scrub ,
comma-separated.
.TP
.BI \-mailbox " mailbox"
Mailbox for
.B mailbox_delete
and
.BR expunge ,
by name or id.
.TP
.BI \-uids " list"
UIDs for
.BR expunge ,
comma-separated.
.TP
.B \-deleted
.B expunge
takes every message flagged
.IR \eDeleted .
.TP
.B \-wait
Wait until the job ends. The exit code is then the job's outcome.
.TP
.BI \-poll " duration"
How often
.B \-wait
asks. Default:
.IR 2s .
.TP
.BI \-idempotency-key " key"
Repeating a request with the same key returns the job the first request
created instead of starting a second one. A different request with the
same key is refused.
.TP
.BI \-account " account"
.TQ
.BI \-state " state"
.TQ
.BI \-limit " n"
.TQ
.BI \-after " id"
Narrow and page
.BR "job list" .
A client with an account scope must name an account.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
Is this account's index sound?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl check -wait user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Delete a mailbox: look first, then act.
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan -mailbox 'Archive/2019' mailbox_delete user@example.org
shardpostctl apply -wait 20260919T173044Z-38cd01e99e31
.RE
.fi
.PP
Empty the trash of an account for good:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan -mailbox Trash -deleted expunge user@example.org
shardpostctl plan show <plan-id>          # how many, and which UIDs
shardpostctl apply -wait <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
The usage counter looks wrong after an incident:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan quota_recalc user@example.org
shardpostctl apply -wait <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
Search finds nothing although the mail is there: rebuild the index. The
account is locked while this runs, so do it in a quiet window.
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan fts_rebuild user@example.org
shardpostctl apply -wait <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
Repair only what the check found, not everything:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan -classes refs,orphans scrub user@example.org
shardpostctl apply -wait <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
Offboarding: remove every trace of an account from the store (the
identity stays in LDAP):
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan purge user@example.org
shardpostctl plan show <plan-id>          # mailboxes, messages, shares
shardpostctl apply -wait <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
Retry an apply safely from a script, without risking a second run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl apply -idempotency-key nightly-2026-09-20 <plan-id>
.RE
.fi
.PP
What is running right now, and what happened to a job?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl job list -account user@example.org
shardpostctl job show 20260919T173049Z-a26a9aabfc44
shardpostctl job cancel 20260919T173049Z-a26a9aabfc44
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Without
.BR \-wait ,
the exit code only says whether the request was accepted. With
.B \-wait
(and for
.BR "job wait" )
it is the outcome of the job:
.TP
.B 0
The job succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The job partly failed; its errors are printed.
.TP
.B 65
The plan was already applied, has expired, or the account drifted from
it.
.TP
.B 67
No such job, plan or account.
.TP
.B 69
The job failed or was cancelled.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role of this kind.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1),
.BR shardpostctl-export (1),
.BR shardpostctl-mailbox (1),
.BR shardpostctl-message (1)
